-- P0.4 — close the RPC door: no anonymous caller may reach a writing SQL function (2026-09-27)
--
-- Measured on prod before this migration (pg_proc, schema public, owner postgres, not trigger functions):
--   1231 RPC-callable functions; 499 signatures (491 names) WRITE — direct INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE,
--   dynamic SQL carrying DML, REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW, DDL, cron.schedule, net.http_post, or calling a writer.
--   Only VOLATILE functions count (Postgres refuses writes inside STABLE/IMMUTABLE ones).
--   anon can EXECUTE 426 of those writing signatures (181 SECURITY DEFINER, 371 with no auth.uid()/auth.role()/is_admin reference);
--   authenticated can EXECUTE 485.
--   Every one of them is reachable at /rest/v1/rpc/<name> with the public anon key.
--
-- After this migration:
--   anon-executable writing signatures 426 -> 5; authenticated-executable 485 -> 73.
--   service_role keeps EXECUTE everywhere (edge functions and cron): every writer already lists it in its ACL
--   (0 rely on the implicit PUBLIC grant), and the GRANT below makes that explicit and idempotent.
--
-- Classes (per function NAME; every overload gets the same treatment):
--   (a) KEEP anon + authenticated — deliberate signed-out writes on public pages (4 names):
--       analyze_organization_data_signals: callee of get_effective_org_config (INVOKER chain runs as anon); updates only the org's own cached data_signals
--       get_effective_org_config: public org profile tabs (INVOKER); calls analyze_organization_data_signals to cache the org's own signals
--       register_make_model_subject: cohort registration from /cohort/:make/:model/:year and universal-search; idempotent, bounded to canonical make/model/year
--       validate_data_room_access_code: L'Officiel data-room gate on the public org profile: outside partners without accounts enter a code; the write is the attempt log
--   (b) REVOKE anon, keep authenticated — called by the web app in signed-in flows (53 names)
--       + 1 pulled in because an INVOKER function kept for authenticated calls them: approve_ownership_verification
--       Visible change for signed-out visitors: ensure_field_evidence — signed-out vehicle pages no longer backfill sparse field_evidence (they still show what exists); log_usage_metric — signed-out visitors no longer write usage_metrics telemetry (hook swallows the error); update_organization_profile_stats — signed-out org pages no longer recompute the org stat cache on view (stored stats still render); join_stream — live-stream viewer join/chat as a visitor (LiveStreamViewer is imported nowhere — dormant); add_chat_message — same as join_stream; generate_invite_code — /intake invite-code generation needs a signed-in business owner (it already requires p_created_by)
--       FINDINGS — 35 of these do no auth check of their own, so any signed-in account can run them
--       (deduct_cash_from_user, admin_* / verify_shop / merge_duplicate_vehicles, create_notification for any user, …):
--       add_activity_feed_item, add_chat_message, add_dynamic_vehicle_field, admin_approve_ownership_verification, admin_reject_ownership_verification, approve_ownership_verification, approve_pending_assignment, award_achievement, backfill_user_profile_stats, backfill_work_sessions_from_photos, create_notification, create_user_request, deduct_cash_from_user, derive_work_sessions, ensure_field_evidence, finalize_work_session, generate_invite_code, generate_spending_analytics, increment_device_image_count, increment_document_stat, join_stream, log_contribution, log_quick_action, log_vehicle_edit, mark_all_notifications_read, mark_notification_read, merge_duplicate_vehicles, reject_pending_assignment, relink_testimony, unmerge_vehicle, update_follow_roi_tracking, update_organization_profile_stats, update_user_profile_stats, update_vehicle_relationship, verify_shop
--   (ios) REVOKE anon, keep authenticated — called by the Swift capture app (apps/nuke-capture-mac + iOS trees on disk) (8 names):
--       add_photo_comment, attribute_image_session, confirm_work_session, record_interaction, record_owner_contribution, request_account_deletion, set_vehicle_build_image, sync_local_vision_tags
--       name suggests the capture app but no Swift source calls it (kept for authenticated anyway, listed): backfill_work_sessions_from_photos, derive_work_sessions, finalize_work_session, increment_device_image_count
--   (c) REVOKE PUBLIC, anon, authenticated — not called by the web app or the capture app (421 names):
--       edge functions and cron reach them as service_role / postgres. Includes the vehicle_images writers
--       (merge_vehicle_into_primary_by_url, correct_image_provenance, retag_image, fix_vehicle_images_for_vehicle,
--       reconcile_vehicle_attribution, …), correct_vehicle_sale_provenance_batch, and process_tier1_batch (web-app
--       admin button, but SECURITY INVOKER with a service-role JWT literal in its body — closed until rewritten).
--
-- Default privileges: pg_default_acl for role postgres in schema public granted EXECUTE on new functions to
--   anon, authenticated, service_role, postgres ({postgres=X/postgres,anon=X/postgres,authenticated=X/postgres,service_role=X/postgres}).
--   Changed below so a NEW function is closed to anon/authenticated until a migration grants it. (supabase_admin has
--   the same default ACL; postgres cannot alter it — functions created by the platform itself keep the old default.)
--   Rule from here on: a reader RPC the web app calls needs `GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION f(...) TO anon, authenticated;`
--   in its migration; a writer needs `TO authenticated` only, and must check auth.uid() itself.
--
-- Not touched: trigger functions (not callable through RPC), functions owned by supabase_admin (extensions),
--   readers (RLS still governs what they return), and RLS policies / views (none reference a writer — checked).
-- P2 pointer: these function bodies embed a secret-shaped literal and must be rewritten when keys rotate:
--   process_tier1_batch, sync_active_bat_external_listings
--
-- Reversal: GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION <sig> TO anon, authenticated; and ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES ... GRANT EXECUTE ON
--   FUNCTIONS TO anon, authenticated. Names and classes are listed in the arrays below.

BEGIN;
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '10s';
SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '120s';
SET LOCAL search_path = public, pg_temp;

-- 0. New functions are closed by default.
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES FOR ROLE postgres IN SCHEMA public REVOKE EXECUTE ON FUNCTIONS FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated;

